  Deadline, GPL-2.0; Garner's Modern American Usage; Richard Nordquist; David
  Foster Wallace).

style/data/norms/lancaster-perceptual.tsv is derived from the Lancaster
Sensorimotor Norms: Lynott, D., Connell, L., Brysbaert, M., Brand, J., &
Carney, J. (2020). The Lancaster Sensorimotor Norms: multidimensional measures
of perceptual and action strength for 40,000 English words. Behavior Research
Methods, 52, 1271-1291. https://doi.org/10.3758/s13428-019-01316-z. Data from
https://osf.io/7emr6/ (file Lancaster_sensorimotor_norms_for_39707_words.csv,
sha256 445d363fb1f9f3e50b86d88e2f46cdc9a22b5dd8a713ce4e7be2a773d57f43c5,
retrieved 2026-10-16), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Changes: single words only, lowercased; only words whose strongest perceptual
modality rates at least 3.5 and leads the next modality by at least 0.5, not
counting interoception as the next modality of a haptic word; columns reduced
to that modality, its mean strength and that lead, in floored tenths of a
rating point using decimal arithmetic. The authors do not endorse writemorebetter.

style/data/norms/concreteness.tsv is writemorebetter's own table, licensed MIT
OR Apache-2.0. Its ratings are AI-generated: they were generated on 2026-10-20
by prompting Anthropic's claude-opus-5-5, claude-sonnet-5-5 and claude-fable-5-1
(three samples each) with writemorebetter's own instructions
(bench/style/concreteness/prompt.txt, sha256
0317ef4beee2b11db9719e811af732839d40536bfaac54b1d20266922b990871) over the
lemma list in style/data/baselines/overused-words.json
(bench/style/concreteness/words.tsv and words-supplement.tsv), averaged across
models, and mapped to a 1-5 scale by a linear fit to a calibration split of
the concreteness ratings in the Glasgow Norms: Scott, G. G., Keitel, A.,
Becirspahic, M., Yao, B., & Sereno, S. C. (2019). The Glasgow Norms: Ratings of
5,500 words on nine scales. Behavior Research Methods, 51, 1258-1270.
https://doi.org/10.3758/s13428-018-1099-3. Data from https://osf.io/42s65/
(file GlasgowNorms.xlsx, sha256
9e3295f4c804289fdd5fa36f2c5fe415826bef3d839702deedd51641b3ff9a39), licensed
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). No Glasgow ratings are included
in the table. No data from Brysbaert, Warriner & Kuperman (2014) was used. The
Glasgow Norms authors do not endorse writemorebetter.

style/data/norms/not-sensory.txt, style/data/suppressed.txt, style/data/fixed-wording.txt,
style/data/literal-guards.txt and style/data/open-slot.txt are writemorebetter's
own lists (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

The word lists in style/data/dialogue/ were written for writemorebetter and are
not taken from any third-party source.

style/data/baselines/overused-words.json is derived from the Google Books Ngram
Viewer English Fiction 1-grams, version 20200217
(https://storage.googleapis.com/books/ngrams/books/datasetsv3.html), retrieved
2026-10-16, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/). writemorebetter summed match
counts for edition years 1990-2019, lemmatized the part-of-speech-tagged forms
with its own tokenizer, merged British spelling variants into their American
lemma, and kept rates per million words, rounded to three significant digits,
for content lemmas at or above one per million
(bench/style/overused_baseline.py). Google does not endorse writemorebetter.

style/data/pacing/cognition.txt is an original writemorebetter lemma list,
version 1 (2026-10-16), licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. It is not derived from
third-party dictionaries or rule resources.

Transition inventory (style/data/transitions.tsv): written for writemorebetter, 2026.
